            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for by chance, then the Sanskrit for turns out well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पाशकः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पाशकः — pāśakaḥ — \"a die\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि पाशकः षट् दर्शयति, तर्हि त्वं जयसि। yadi pāśakaḥ ṣaṭ darśayati, tarhi tvaṃ jayasi. If the die shows six, you win."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पाशकः (pāśakaḥ) is built on pāśa, \"a cord, a noose\", with the ending -ka; MW gives pāśaka as a snare, and also as a die (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
