        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: हारयति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हारयति — hārayati — \"loses at play\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि त्वं द्यूतं क्रीडसि, तर्हि त्वं धनं हारयसि। yadi tvaṃ dyūtaṃ krīḍasi, tarhi tvaṃ dhanaṃ hārayasi. If you gamble, you lose money."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः सर्वं धनं हारितवान्, saḥ sarvaṃ dhanaṃ hāritavān."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Future: हारयिष्यति, hārayiṣyati."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हारयति (hārayati) comes from the causative of the root √hṛ, \"to take, to carry off\": MW gives it as to have a thing taken from oneself, to lose it, above all at play (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
